    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah its just hard to see a way out. like i do all the \"right\" things. i work the hours, i try to budget, i do everything i'm \"supposed\" to do but it's like the system is just designed to keep me underwater. what's the point of trying to build a future if the cost of existing is just more debt and more stress? it feels like there's no actual win state. just like... a long, slow drain.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is deeply demoralizing when you do everything \"right\" and still feel like you're sinking. That feeling that the system is rigged against you is a very real and heavy burden to carry every day. When the goalposts keep moving, it makes the idea of a \"win\" feel like a cruel joke. Maybe the point isn't to win the race, but to find a way to stop running so hard that you break.",
      "source": "target",
